<div class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-6xl flex-col gap-6">
  <%= render FlatPack::PageTitle::Component.new(
    title: "Config",
    subtitle: "Tune the host-app actor lookup, layouts, public controller overrides, and redirect behavior.",
    variant: :h1
  ) %>

  <div class="space-y-8">
    <section class="space-y-4">
      <%= render FlatPack::SectionTitle::Component.new(
        title: "Available settings",
        subtitle: "These are the primary configuration points exposed by the addon."
      ) %>

      <div class="space-y-3 text-sm leading-7 text-(--surface-muted-content-color)">
        <p><strong>management_authorizer</strong> (required) decides whether a user may edit publishable content. Receives <code>recording:</code> and <code>actor:</code> keyword args.</p>
        <p><strong>layout</strong> (optional) sets the layout for all gem-managed screens (default: <code>"application"</code>).</p>
        <p><strong>register_public_renderer</strong> (optional, repeatable) maps a recordable type to a host controller/action/layout for published routes.</p>
        <p><strong>canonical_redirect_status</strong> (optional) sets the status code for stale slug redirects (default: <code>:moved_permanently</code>).</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <%= render FlatPack::SectionTitle::Component.new(
        title: "Initializer example",
        subtitle: "The generated initializer shows the intended extension points."
      ) %>

      <%= render FlatPack::CodeBlock::Component.new(
        language: :ruby,
        code: <<~RUBY
          RecordingStudioPublishable.configure do |config|
            config.register_public_renderer(
              "Page",
              controller: "pages",
              action: :show
            )

            config.register_public_renderer(
              "Article",
              controller: "articles",
              action: :show
            )

            config.management_authorizer = lambda do |recording:, actor:, **|
              actor.present? && recording.present? && actor.email == "admin@admin.com"
            end
          end
        RUBY
      ) %>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <%= render FlatPack::SectionTitle::Component.new(
        title: "Related guidance",
        subtitle: "These settings work together with the install generator and the public route helpers."
      ) %>

      <div class="space-y-3 text-sm leading-7 text-(--surface-muted-content-color)">
        <p>Use the host app initializer to tailor authorization, layouts, and the backend controller/action that each published recordable type should resolve through.</p>
        <p>The published URL stays the same; the controller mapping only changes which host controller/action prepares the page.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</div>
